{"code":"47-2152.00","title":"Plumbers, Pipefitters, and Steamfitters","description":"Assemble, install, alter, and repair pipelines or pipe systems that carry water, steam, air, or other liquids or gases. May install heating and cooling equipment and mechanical control systems. Includes sprinkler fitters.","jobZone":3,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.5952},"I":{"score":2.2,"share":0.119},"A":{"score":1,"share":0},"S":{"score":1.16,"share":0.0159},"E":{"score":1,"share":0},"C":{"score":3.72,"share":0.2698}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":23469,"text":"Shut off steam, water, or other gases or liquids from pipe sections, using valve keys or wrenches.","core":true,"importance":4.19,"relevance":88.22,"frequency":4.13},{"id":23478,"text":"Install underground storm, sanitary, or water piping systems, extending piping as needed to connect fixtures and plumbing.","core":true,"importance":4.18,"relevance":96.35,"frequency":3.63},{"id":23466,"text":"Assemble pipe sections, tubing, or fittings, using couplings, clamps, screws, bolts, cement, plastic solvent, caulking, or soldering, brazing, or welding equipment.","core":true,"importance":4.16,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.06},{"id":23474,"text":"Locate and mark the position of pipe installations, connections, passage holes, or fixtures in structures, using measuring instruments such as rulers or levels.","core":true,"importance":4.14,"relevance":99.79,"frequency":5.3},{"id":23459,"text":"Cut, thread, or hammer pipes to specifications, using tools such as saws, cutting torches, pipe threaders, or pipe benders.","core":true,"importance":4.12,"relevance":98.92,"frequency":5.36},{"id":23460,"text":"Lay out full scale drawings of pipe systems, supports, or related equipment, according to blueprints.","core":true,"importance":4.11,"relevance":81.44,"frequency":4.7},{"id":23462,"text":"Plan pipe system layout, installation, or repair, according to specifications.","core":true,"importance":4.07,"relevance":91.06,"frequency":4.37},{"id":23475,"text":"Review blueprints, building codes, or specifications to determine work details or procedures.","core":true,"importance":4.05,"relevance":99.59,"frequency":4.41},{"id":23465,"text":"Select pipe sizes, types, or related materials, such as supports, hangers, or hydraulic cylinders, according to specifications.","core":true,"importance":4.03,"relevance":91.29,"frequency":4.99},{"id":23472,"text":"Fill pipes or plumbing fixtures with water or air and observe pressure gauges to detect and locate leaks.","core":true,"importance":4.02,"relevance":99.78,"frequency":3.46},{"id":23471,"text":"Direct helpers engaged in pipe cutting, preassembly, or installation of plumbing systems or components.","core":true,"importance":4.01,"relevance":94.72,"frequency":4.95},{"id":23461,"text":"Inspect, examine, or test installed systems or pipe lines, using pressure gauge, hydrostatic testing, observation, or other methods.","core":true,"importance":3.99,"relevance":88.06,"frequency":3.63},{"id":23467,"text":"Install pipe assemblies, fittings, valves, appliances such as dishwashers or water heaters, or fixtures such as sinks or toilets, using hand or power tools.","core":true,"importance":3.99,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.57},{"id":23476,"text":"Anchor steel supports from ceiling joists to hold pipes in place.","core":true,"importance":3.93,"relevance":92.76,"frequency":4.56},{"id":23463,"text":"Attach pipes to walls, structures, or fixtures, such as radiators or tanks, using brackets, clamps, tools, or welding equipment.","core":true,"importance":3.92,"relevance":81.71,"frequency":4.84},{"id":23464,"text":"Modify, clean, or maintain pipe systems, units, fittings, or related machines or equipment, using hand or power tools.","core":true,"importance":3.81,"relevance":76.34,"frequency":4.33},{"id":23468,"text":"Install automatic controls to regulate pipe systems.","core":true,"importance":3.73,"relevance":70.98,"frequency":3.47},{"id":23470,"text":"Keep records of work assignments.","core":true,"importance":3.73,"relevance":87.25,"frequency":4.52},{"id":23477,"text":"Estimate time, material, or labor costs for use in project plans.","core":true,"importance":3.73,"relevance":81.31,"frequency":3.99},{"id":23479,"text":"Inspect structures to assess material or equipment needs, to establish the sequence of pipe installations, or to plan installation around obstructions, such as electrical wiring.","core":true,"importance":3.66,"relevance":97.55,"frequency":3.83},{"id":23473,"text":"Maintain or repair plumbing by replacing defective washers, replacing or mending broken pipes, or opening clogged drains.","core":true,"importance":3.62,"relevance":93.43,"frequency":4.21},{"id":23488,"text":"Repair or remove and replace system components.","core":true,"importance":3.6,"relevance":89.47,"frequency":3.51},{"id":23481,"text":"Cut openings in structures to accommodate pipes or pipe fittings, using hand or power tools.","core":true,"importance":3.57,"relevance":98.61,"frequency":4.22},{"id":23482,"text":"Inspect work sites for obstructions or holes that could cause structural weakness.","core":false,"importance":3.56,"relevance":42.45,"frequency":3.95},{"id":23484,"text":"Install pipe systems to support alternative energy-fueled systems, such as geothermal heating or cooling systems.","core":false,"importance":3.38,"relevance":64.09,"frequency":3.44},{"id":23483,"text":"Install fixtures, appliances, or equipment designed to reduce water or energy consumption.","core":false,"importance":3.3,"relevance":57.15,"frequency":3.4},{"id":23487,"text":"Repair hydraulic or air pumps.","core":false,"importance":3.22,"relevance":42.47,"frequency":2.36},{"id":23480,"text":"Install green plumbing equipment, such as faucet flow restrictors, dual-flush or pressure-assisted flush toilets, or tankless hot water heaters.","core":true,"importance":3.09,"relevance":96.68,"frequency":2.94},{"id":23485,"text":"Weld small pipes or special piping, using specialized t